// bubbler profile: thunderbird
//
// Mail is a network and somewhere to save an attachment: `network` for
// the servers you configure, `home-share "Downloads"` for what you save
// out of a message. Everything else — the profile, the message store,
// the address book — lives in the private home.
//
// Gecko has defaulted to Wayland since Firefox 121 and takes the display
// from the `wayland` grant, so no `env` node sets MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND;
// `env MOZ_ENABLE_WAYLAND="0"` goes back to Xwayland.
//
// Bare by design. Add:
//   dri
//     — the GPU. Without it Gecko composites in software, which is enough
//       for a mail window and slower for a video in one.
//   dbus
//   portals
//     — the file chooser that reaches outside the shared directories: the
//       portal runs it on the host and exports what you pick into this
//       instance's document view. Without them the chooser is the one
//       inside the sandbox and sees the private home and ~/Downloads.
//   notify
//     — new-mail notifications and calendar alarms. Needs `dbus`.
wayland
network
home-share "Downloads" mode=rw
desktop "org.mozilla.Thunderbird.desktop"
command "thunderbird"
